-(none yet)
+- Compute estimate: the figure above (6 to 7 minutes per run, about 7 hours in total) was wrong. The measured
+  figure for the 64-run main batch is 30.6 compute-hours (mean 1539 s training plus 183 s evaluation per run),
+  about 8 to 11 hours of wall-clock time with four runs in parallel. This does not affect any design decision.
+- Run records show `git_dirty: true`, because the working tree had uncommitted changes to generated egg-info
+  files (not source code) when the batch started. The commit hash in each record is 5f0550f.
+
+## Extensions added after the main results (28 November 2026)
+The main batch was run and analysed first (H1, H2 and H3 all met their frozen thresholds; the history agents
+did not beat the best fixed two-drug cycle). Three objections to that result were then identified, and
+three extension batches were added to answer them. They are EXPLORATORY: they were decided after seeing the
+main results, they do not change or replace any frozen hypothesis, and the paper reports them as such.
+- E1, longer training (configs/ext_long): history and state agents at delay 2 and the repository agent at
+  delay 0, 1500 episodes, seeds 10 to 14. Question: does more training close the gap between the history
+  agent and the best fixed cycle?
+- E2, convolutional front end (configs/ext_conv): state, history and decoy agents at delay 2, 500 episodes,
+  seeds 10 to 14, using the repository agent's convolutional layers on the flat observation. Question: is
+  the main result an artefact of the Dense network?
+- E3, more seeds (configs/ext_seeds): seeds 15 to 17 for delays 1 and 3 (state, history, decoy), so every
+  condition in the main comparison has 8 seeds.
+All other settings are identical to the main batch. Configurations are generated by
+scripts/make_extension_configs.py.
